    "created_at": "2019-02-13T18:06:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-02-13T18:06:42Z",
    "body": "What Gecko actually implements is that we have a \"channel\" data structure that sort of corresponds to both a request and a response.  This data structure has a getter for a property named \"contentDispositionFilename\".  For HTTP channels this queries the \"Content-Disposition\" header, if any.  For blob channels it looks at what the filename was on the thing the blob url was created from, if any.  We use the same infrastructure to implement `<a download>` also...\r\n\r\nI think those are the only three consumers in Gecko at the moment.\r\n\r\nSo the other option in spec terms is to simply have a suggested filename as a property of a Response and set it from whatever information sources are involved...",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
